# Component and Design System Conventions

## Design System (@sig/ui)

All shared UI primitives live in `packages/ui/src/`. Import as:

```typescript
import { Button, Card, Badge, Dialog } from "@sig/ui";
```

Never install competing UI libraries (Chakra, MUI, Ant Design, etc.).
If a primitive is missing from `@sig/ui`, add it there rather than building
a one-off in `apps/web`.

## Component Declaration

Use function declarations with named exports:

```typescript
interface SignalCardProps {
  signal: Signal;
  onArchive?: (id: string) => void;
  className?: string;
}

function SignalCard({ signal, onArchive, className }: SignalCardProps) {
  return (
    <Card className={cn("p-4", className)}>
      <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
        <h3 className="font-medium text-foreground">{signal.title}</h3>
        <Badge variant={signal.priority === "high" ? "destructive" : "secondary"}>
          {signal.priority}
        </Badge>
      </div>
      <p className="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">{signal.description}</p>
    </Card>
  );
}

export { SignalCard };
```

## Org-Scoping Pattern

All data-fetching components must be org-scoped. Never fetch across organizations:

```typescript
// Server component
async function ProjectList() {
  const orgId = await getOrgIdFromSession();
  const projects = await getProjectsByOrg(orgId);
  return <ProjectGrid projects={projects} />;
}

// Client component with Firestore hook
function SignalList() {
  const { orgId } = useAuth();
  const signals = useCollection<Signal>(`orgs/${orgId}/signals`, {
    orderBy: ["createdAt", "desc"],
    limit: 50,
  });
  // ...
}
```

## Server vs Client Components

Default to server components. Add `"use client"` only for:
- Components with `useState`, `useEffect`, event handlers
- Components using Firestore real-time listeners (`onSnapshot`)
- Components using `useAuth()` context
- Interactive form components

Keep client components small and push them to leaf nodes.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS only. Use `cn()` for conditional classes.
- Semantic color tokens from the design system: `text-foreground`, `bg-background`,
  `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-accent`, `border-border`, `text-destructive`.
- Always include dark mode variants for custom styles.
- Responsive: mobile-first with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` breakpoints.

## Component Variants (cva)

For components with multiple visual variants, use `class-variance-authority`:

```typescript
import { cva, type VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority";

const badgeVariants = cva(
  "inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold",
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        default: "bg-primary text-primary-foreground",
        secondary: "bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground",
        destructive: "bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground",
        outline: "border border-border text-foreground",
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: "default",
    },
  }
);
```

## Loading States

Use skeleton components that match the final layout:

```typescript
function SignalCardSkeleton() {
  return (
    <Card className="p-4">
      <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
        <Skeleton className="h-5 w-48" />
        <Skeleton className="h-5 w-16 rounded-full" />
      </div>
      <Skeleton className="mt-2 h-4 w-full" />
    </Card>
  );
}
```

## Accessibility

- Interactive elements must be keyboard accessible.
- Use semantic HTML (`button`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `article`).
- Icon-only buttons require `aria-label`.
- Form inputs require associated labels.
- Color must not be the sole indicator of state.

## Testing

- Test user behavior, not implementation.
- Use Testing Library queries: `getByRole` > `getByLabelText` > `getByText`.
- Colocate tests: `SignalCard.test.tsx` next to `SignalCard.tsx`.
- Mock Firestore hooks in component tests.
